converge.prompt:
Ticket:

${ticket}

Change (in ${worktrees.repo.path}, branch ${worktrees.repo.branch}):

${change}

Review it: does it do what the ticket asked, is it the right shape, what would you send back. Be specific and terse — file and line where you can.

Ticket (the acceptance criteria):

${ticket}

Change to validate (in ${worktrees.repo.path}, branch ${worktrees.repo.branch}):

${change}

Exercise it and report PASS or FAIL with concrete evidence — what you ran, what you saw. A FAIL must name the case that fails.

phases.prompt:
Open a pull request for the change below.

Ticket:

${ticket}

Change:

${change}

Review + QA verdict:

${verdict}

The change is committed on branch ${worktrees.repo.branch} in ${worktrees.repo.path} (a worktree of the repository). Push it (`git push -u origin ${worktrees.repo.branch}`) and open the PR from it. Title it from the ticket. In the body, summarise the change, link the ticket, and quote the QA evidence. Do not open the PR if the verdict asked for changes — say so instead.
